WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.440
Most triple A titles these days are pretty predictable.

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:03.520
You have the Hero,

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:04.080
the Villain,

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.300
the polite dialog choice,

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.660
the rude dialog choice,

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:07.440
the bad guys,

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.300
the good guys,

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.320
and all the meaningless choices along the way.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:14.480
If you're watching my videos then you should already know that Dark Souls breaks the mold.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.500
Most games either have a one canon ending,

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:21.460
or allow you to choose from a selection of moral mind filled endings at the end of the game.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.440
Dark Souls is the latter but the endings are ambiguous as hell.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:29.340
The more you learn about the game the more confusing the endings become.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:33.840
Most games give you closure but both Dark Souls endings probably leave you wondering;

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.160
What would happen next?

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.000
What consequence would my choice have in the game world?

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:41.620
The first ending we'll analyse is the 'Link the Fire' ending

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:45.120
You sacrifice your body and soul as fuel for the first Flame,

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:46.700
which keeps the gods in power.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:48.760
We'll call this the 'Light ending'.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:53.340
Your other choice is letting the Flame die out, allowing you to become the Dark Lord

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.180
and ushering in the Age of Man.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.260
Lets call this the 'Dark ending'.

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:02.180
Now this video assumes you have some idea of what's going on in the Dark Souls universe.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:05.380
If you don't I have a Dark Souls Lore in a minute video you could watch,

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:08.540
or you can brush up on the fundamentals presented by EpicNameBro.

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:12.900
To properly understand the endings you must understand what makes them significant.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:16.520
In the beginning the Four Lords Souls were found within the first Flame.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:21.000
Gywn obtained the Light Soul and ushered in an Age of Fire based around that first Flame.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:25.400
This Age of Fire meant that the gods and the lords were in control of the world.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:26.620
Ruling over humanity.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:30.320
They lit bonfires from the first Flame and shepherded the humans.

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:32.460
But.. where did the humans come from?

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:36.560
Well, it's my theory that humanity is spawned from the fragments of the Dark Soul.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.840
As humanity split and grew and split and grew,

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.840
The Dark began to overcome the Light.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:45.320
This concept of Disparity plays a huge role in the game.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:48.280
As the first Flame faded the Light faded,

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:51.880
and as the Light faded the power of Gwyn and the Age of Fire faded.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:57.080
As the gods started to lose their power, they began to recognize the threat that humanity could pose.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.220
It seems the gods couldn't decide what to make of humanity.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:04.480
In the dialog's of Ciaran and Gough we see some of this uncertainty.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:07.820
If you aid them, they decide that humans aren't so bad after all.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:11.780
But if you slight them, then they treat you with that built up resentment.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:13.140
"Hhgaaa...

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:17.460
So this.. is true human nature."

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:21.520
The Flame continues to fade.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:26.460
The gods abandon Anor Londo, and the remaining gods use illusions to preserve their power.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:31.700
Gywn, holder of the Light Soul goes to the Kiln of the first Flame and offers himself as fuel.

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:35.060
He sacrifices himself to let the Flame burn a little longer.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:38.600
This buys the gods a bit more time to find the solution to their problem.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:40.920
You are that solution.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:44.360
By linking the fire, you become the fuel for the first Flame.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:47.240
With you in Gywn's place, the age of fire can continue.

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:49.440
But what makes you so special?

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:50.120
Well,

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:53.720
the character is a very powerful undead if they can make it all the way to Gywn.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:57.140
and it follows that the more powerful you are the longer you will burn.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:01.040
It could be that this is why Frampt is trying to push undead towards Gywn.

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:04.020
He's trying to find the one who will burn the longest.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:10.000
So by burning in Gywn's place you have to ask yourself what purpose it serves.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:14.060
You're preserving the reign of the gods and rising to the needs of a dying hierarchy.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:16.600
It's not even a temporary solution.

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:21.560
Gywn was powerful enough to take out the immortal dragons and even he became a husk by the end.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:24.800
So while you could see linking the flame as a selfless act,

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:27.680
it's hard to imagine that you're doing it for any greater purpose.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:32.700
Indeed, if you link the Flame you are rising to the needs of people who could simply be using you.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:35.220
So, is this the good ending?

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.380
At first glance it seems like it.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:40.620
Most players go through the game only meeting the serpent Frampt,

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:43.760
who promises that linking the flame will undo the curse of the undead.

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:46.240
He talks of fate and gives you purpose.

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:49.020
So at first I thought this was the right thing to do.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:52.240
I didn't know that Anor Londo and Gwynevere were illusions.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:55.880
I didn't know I was being used and I thought I was being selfless.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.880
But then I head what Kaathe had to say.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:02.440
He says that after the advent of fire, the ancient Lords found three souls.

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:06.200
But your progenitor found the Dark Soul and waited for fire to subside.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:09.560
He says that with the fading Flame comes the age of Man.

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:12.780
He paints Gywn as a god who resisted the course of nature.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:16.980
And says that you are being manipulated by Frampt to keep Gywn's age of Fire going.

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:20.520
By killing Gwyn and walking away from the first Flame,

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:25.220
Kaathe promises that the Dark will finally come and with it the age of Man will begin.

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:29.540
At first I thought that Kaathe's hidden dialog was the truth.

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:30.760
It makes sense.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:33.260
When you realize that Frampt is manipulating you,

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:36.040
you feel like you should believe everything Kaathe has to say.

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:38.700
It seems like Kaathe is telling the whole truth.

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:40.480
But, is he telling the whole truth?

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:43.580
Is the darkness really a place where humans can thrive?

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:47.040
Humans are born from the Dark Soul, that much is true.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:49.360
The black humanity sprite is proof of that.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:52.460
But when we journey back to see what happened in Oolacile.

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:55.380
We realize how dangerous the Dark is to humans.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:57.800
Oolacile was once a human city,

00:04:57.860 --> 00:04:59.180
overrun by the Dark.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:03.760
These are it's residence and this is the fate of the humans who come into contact with the Dark.

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:06.760
This is the age of Man that Kaathe promises.

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:10.100
One serpent tells you lies and the other tells you truth.

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:12.280
Both of them are manipulating you.

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:13.500
If you link the Fire,

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:18.820
you are sacrificing yourself so that Frampt and Gwyndolin can rule with the illusion of power in Anor Londo.

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:22.040
If you let the Flame fade, the age of Dark will come.

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:24.640
But is this a place where humans thrive?

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:25.400
No,

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:27.200
Oolacile is proof of that.

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:30.020
In the end it doesn't matter what you do.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:32.840
If you link the Flame you're just delaying the inevitable.

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:34.320
If you let the Flame fade,

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.020
the Darkness comes a little sooner.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:37.300
With you at the helm.

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:41.840
The one cannon ending to Dark Souls is in the prologue.

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:43.900
One day the Flame will fade,

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:46.080
and only Dark will remain.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:50.840
So instead of choosing an ending just go and live with Priscilla or something.

